        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): keep OpenAI tool call id truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`normalizeToolCallId` in `openai-completions.ts:1052` truncates oversized OpenAI tool call IDs with `id.slice(0, 40)`. When a tool call ID contains a UTF-16 surrogate pair straddling positions 39-40, `slice` splits the pair and leaves an unpaired high surrogate — producing **invalid Unicode in the outbound API request**.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`String.prototype.slice(0, 40)` operates on UTF-16 code units. A surrogate pair (e.g. 🐱 `\\uD83D\\uDC31`) consumes 2 code units. The fix switches to `truncateUtf16Safe(id, 40)` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`, an existing repo helper.\n\n## Full pipeline proof (addresses ClawSweeper P1)\n\nThe test **no longer throws in `onPayload`**. The mock OpenAI client returns a valid streaming response, and the entire pipeline completes through `create→withResponse→stream→result()`.\n\n### Test output (47/47 pass)\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  47 passed (47)\n```\n\n### BEFORE (old test) — `onPayload` throws, aborts before `fetch`\n\n```\nexpect(result.stopReason).toBe(\"error\");  // onPayload threw\n// client.chat.completions.create was NEVER called\n```\n\n### AFTER (new test) — full pipeline completes\n\n```\nexpect(result.stopReason).toBe(\"stop\");   // stream completed naturally\n// client.chat.completions.create was called with valid payload\n```\n\n### API client proof\n\nThe test additionally verifies that the normalized `tool_call_id` reached `client.chat.completions.create` via `mockOpenAIOptionsRef.payloads`:\n\n```typescript\nconst lastPayload = mockOpenAIOptionsRef.payloads[mockOpenAIOptionsRef.payloads.length - 1];\nexpect(lastPayload).toBeDefined();\nconst apiToolMessage = apiMessages.find((m) => m.role === \"tool\");\nexpect(apiToolMessage.tool_call_id).toBe(normalizedId); // same safe id\n```\n\nThis proves the payload went through the complete code path — `buildParams` → `onPayload` → `create()` → `withResponse()` → `stream.result()` — not just captured mid-pipeline.\n\n## Outbound payload proof\n\nInput: 41-code-unit tool call ID with 🐱 surrogate pair at positions 39-40.\n\n### BEFORE fix (`id.slice(0, 40)`) — BROKEN\n\n```json\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"tool\",\n      \"tool_call_id\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ud83d\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n- 40 code units, trailing **unpaired high surrogate** `\\uD83D`\n- Invalid Unicode sent to OpenAI API — downstream rejection risk\n\n### AFTER fix (`truncateUtf16Safe(id, 40)`) — SAFE\n\n```json\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"tool\",\n      \"tool_call_id\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n- 39 code units, clean ASCII\n- Valid Unicode in outbound API request\n\n## Evidence Map\n\n| Layer | Detail |\n|-------|--------|\n| **Changed surface** | `normalizeToolCallId` in `openai-completions.ts:1052` — `slice(0,40)` → `truncateUtf16Safe` |\n| **Sibling UTF-16 PRs** | #104054, #107664, #109561, #109498, #109839 — same helper |\n| **Callers** | `convertMessages` → `streamOpenAICompletions` — cross-model tool-call path |\n| **Test** | 47/47 pass; surrogate-pair boundary test with 41-unit 🐱 input |\n| **Mutation proof** | Reverting to `slice` makes test FAIL: `trailing high surrogate: true` |\n| **Full pipeline** | Test no longer throws; mock completes `create→withResponse→stream`; `stopReason === \"stop\"` |\n| **API client proof** | `mockOpenAIOptionsRef.payloads` confirms normalized id reached `client.chat.completions.create` |\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Multi-model `openai` provider tool-call conversations produce valid Unicode in all IDs\n- No change for IDs without surrogate pairs at the 40-unit boundary\n- Non-OpenAI provider paths unchanged",
        "branch": "fix/openai-tool-call-id-utf16-truncation",
